WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
The code is ready. Now come four announcements.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.000
PatchPitch takes one set of facts and drafts for Telegram, X, DEV, and GitHub.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.000
My real local run finished in about two minutes. Five requests, four drafts.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:24.000
The first X attempt was too long. I fixed the writing budget, then kept six relevant tags.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Review the saved results. Switching drafts doesn't ask the model to start over.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:37.000
For the DEV article, Quillgrain supplies the writing brief. I gave the story another editorial pass.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.000
One command. Four drafts. Time to make them yours.
